● Analysis: NeuroFit Advanced Programme

  Context & Purpose:
  This is a comprehensive 12-week fitness program created by Pete Ryan, a
  two-time British kickboxing champion with 18 years of personal training
  experience. The program targets busy professionals and includes ADHD-friendly
  strategies.

  Current Structure:
  - 12-week program divided into 4 phases (Foundation, Strength & Skill,
  Hypertrophy & Conditioning, Power & Peak)
  - 21 detailed sections covering exercises, nutrition, mindset, progress
  tracking
  - Interactive Excel workbook for planning and tracking
  - Specialized sections for fighters and ADHD considerations

● Key Expansion Opportunities Identified:

  1. Beginner-Specific Content - More detailed onboarding for complete beginners
  2. Advanced Specialization Tracks - Sport-specific training paths
  3. Business Professional Integration - Workplace wellness and desk-based
  solutions
  4. Women's Specific Training - Hormonal considerations and pregnancy
  modifications
  5. Senior/Masters Training - Age-appropriate modifications and mobility focus
  6. Mental Health Integration - Deeper dive into anxiety, depression, and
  stress management
  7. Injury Rehabilitation - Return-to-exercise protocols
  8. Competition Preparation - Detailed fight camp and competition protocols
  9. Online Community Platform - Interactive elements and peer support
  10. Certification Program - Training others to deliver NeuroFit principles

